-- title:
--   Mod-𝔪 Galois representation of a Hecke maximal ideal
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, a level $N \ge 1$ with $p \nmid N$, a finite set $S$ of naturals, and a weight $k \in \mathbb{Z}$ together with $k_n \in \mathbb{N}$ satisfying $(k_n : \mathbb{Z}) = k$. Let $\mathbb{T} =$ `heckeAlgebra N k S` be the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}} S_k(\Gamma_0(N))$ generated by the operators `heckeTLin` attached to primes $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \notin S$ and the operators `heckeULin` attached to primes $q \mid N$ with $q \notin S$, and let $\mathfrak{m} \subset \mathbb{T}$ be a maximal ideal containing the image of $p$. Then there are a finite field $L$, a ring homomorphism $j : \mathbb{T}/\mathfrak{m} \to L$ and a group homomorphism $\rho : \operatorname{Aut}_{\mathbb{Q}}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}) \to \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ with the following properties. First, $\rho$ factors through a finite level: there is an intermediate field $\mathbb{Q} \subseteq F \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $F$ finite over $\mathbb{Q}$ such that $\rho(\sigma) = 1$ whenever $\sigma$ fixes $F$ pointwise. Second, for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid N$, $\ell \notin S$ and $\ell \ne p$, every valuation subring $A \subset \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\ell$ a non-unit of $A$, and every $\sigma$ in the decomposition subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ acting on the residue field of $A$ by $x \mapsto x^{\ell}$, the underlying matrix of $\rho(\sigma)$ has trace $j(T_\ell \bmod \mathfrak{m})$, where $T_\ell$ is `heckeAlgebra.T`, and determinant $\ell^{\,k_n - 1}$ in $L$.
--
--   This is Deligne's theorem on Galois representations attached to Hecke eigensystems, in its mod-$\mathfrak{m}$ form and before any descent of the coefficients from the finite field $L$ to the residue field $\mathbb{T}/\mathfrak{m}$ itself; the weight-two case and the case $k \ge 3$ are supplied separately, the latter combined with the Deligne–Serre lifting lemma for the Hecke algebra acting on $S_k(\Gamma_0(N))$. It feeds the construction of the residual representation whose Frobenius traces are prescribed by the Hecke eigenvalues, used in the level-lowering part of the argument.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_GaloisRep_exists_finiteField_galoisRep_trace_eq_heckeT_mod_of_isMaximal.lean

